          "children": [
            {
              "id": "5fe713cd-2f4c-48c1-8ac1-6bfac5d10d1c",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<strong>Alchemy</strong> refers principally to the historical proto-scientific practice of transforming materials, often base metals into precious ones, most notably the <a href=\"#/quest\">quest</a> for the Philosopher's Stone. The practice of alchemy can be understood as a ludic pursuit, as its practitioners engaged in a form of experimental play and mystical exploration, attempting to decode the <a href=\"#/secret\">hidden secrets</a> of the universe as if they were one grand <a href=\"#/puzzle\">puzzle</a>. Alchemy, as a philosophical and spiritual practice, has influenced modern game design and storytelling, often appearing as a recurring theme or mechanic in <a href=\"#/role-playing\">role-playing games</a> and other interactive media, as early as <em><a href=\"#/dungeons-and-dragons\">Dungeons &amp; Dragons</a></em>."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ab85c159-4fb0-4eb6-aeee-440f325c8a35",
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "7fea8f47-216e-4a11-aebc-1ea8302f16e9",
              "type": "image",
              "src": "./assets/images/untitled-52d04d8657ee.webp",
              "caption": "<em>an Alchemy Lab worktable from </em><a href=\"/43617e844e0946c2b0e51d17b77f8704\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><em>The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim</em></a><em>, used to </em><a href=\"#/craft-ing\"><em>craft</em></a><em> potions &amp; poisons</em>",
              "alt": "Untitled"
            },
            {
              "id": "947fac92-3f47-43e6-8768-521f22d2721b",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0afa1aa8-33c2-44cc-a665-5c74888feb54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "In games and play, alchemy often represents a process of transformation, discovery, and experimentation. Players may assume the role of alchemists, using combinations of reagents, symbols, and <a href=\"#/ritual\">rituals</a> to create magical items or achieve specific goals. Alchemy-based mechanics challenge players to explore the boundaries of the <a href=\"#/environment\">game world</a>, engage with its underlying <a href=\"#/logic\">logic</a>, and solve complex puzzles. The alchemical tradition's rich symbolism and <a href=\"#/mystery\">mystery</a> provide an engaging backdrop for <a href=\"#/narrative-7dbd6451\">narratives</a>, contributing to a sense of wonder, <a href=\"#/cabinet-of-curiosities\">curiosity</a>, and playfulness in games."
    },
    {
      "id": "e3007dbc-76d7-47c4-a5e8-7b9ac078939a",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": ""
